WEBVTT

00:14.731 --> 00:19.081
Representing the graduating 
class, Liniana Dedoldia!

00:19.081 --> 00:22.151
And Pursena Adoldia!

00:24.101 --> 00:30.611
I will now confer your diplomas and 
class-D Mages' Guild certifications!

01:51.111 --> 01:57.031
<b>III</b>

01:51.111 --> 01:57.031
<b><i>Mushoku Tensei</i></b>

01:51.111 --> 01:57.031
<b><b><i>Jobless Reincarnation</i></b></b>

01:59.351 --> 02:04.081
I was surprised to see you both at 
Linia and Pursena's graduation.

02:04.081 --> 02:08.711
Despite our differences, 
they have been loyal to you, Master.

02:08.711 --> 02:13.461
That being the case, 
holding a grudge would ill become me.

02:13.851 --> 02:18.321
To be honest, they're so crude, 
I've never had much to do with them,

02:18.321 --> 02:22.711
but as a special student myself, 
I consider them comrades in learning.

02:23.191 --> 02:25.811
So, I wanted to give 
them a proper send-off.

02:27.141 --> 02:33.191
<i>When I got here, none of the special 
students exactly got along.</i>

02:33.951 --> 02:36.081
<i>I guess these guys have changed, too.</i>

02:40.251 --> 02:42.281
Nanahoshi, I'm coming in.

02:42.281 --> 02:43.471
Go ahead.

02:46.691 --> 02:48.471
Did you catch another cold?

02:49.481 --> 02:51.031
Seems like it.

02:51.031 --> 02:55.731
<i>Nanahoshi's health hasn't been 
great for the past year.</i>

02:55.731 --> 02:58.301
<i>Dry coughing, fevers, the works.</i>

02:58.301 --> 03:02.091
<i>I've been treating her 
with magic every time,</i>

03:02.091 --> 03:04.691
<i>but then she gets sick again.</i>

03:04.941 --> 03:08.851
Detoxification magic can't 
fix an unhealthy body.

03:08.851 --> 03:12.571
You should at least rest 
until you fully recover.

03:12.571 --> 03:16.731
I can't lie in bed when my 
research is going so well.

03:16.731 --> 03:19.801
<i>Nanahoshi's right that 
she's making progress.</i>

03:20.151 --> 03:22.301
<i>She's up to phase three now.</i>

03:22.301 --> 03:27.221
<i>The goal is to summon something 
alive, a plant or small animal.</i>

03:27.541 --> 03:31.241
<i>It won't be long before vegetables from 
our old world appear in this one.</i>

03:31.711 --> 03:33.251
<i>This is what I call smooth sailing.</i>

03:33.701 --> 03:36.081
Okay. Time to start the experiment.

03:37.751 --> 03:38.751
Come in.

03:41.941 --> 03:43.361
Ex<i>mew</i>se us.

03:43.361 --> 03:44.651
We're coming in.

03:44.651 --> 03:46.741
Boss, we've been looking for mew.

03:46.741 --> 03:48.961
We'd like a moment of your time.

03:48.961 --> 03:51.911
<i>They seem a little different today.</i>

03:51.911 --> 03:53.471
<i>Do they want another duel?</i>

03:53.921 --> 03:57.731
<i>Maybe they feel like they can't 
leave without beating me.</i>

03:57.731 --> 03:59.791
Come on, Boss.

03:59.791 --> 04:01.221
Do this for us.

04:03.171 --> 04:04.761
<i>Well, why not?</i>

04:04.761 --> 04:06.521
<i>This is goodbye, so I'll play along.</i>

04:06.931 --> 04:08.241
All right.

04:08.481 --> 04:10.451
Nanahoshi, I'll be right back.

04:10.451 --> 04:13.481
I asked you first. 
What about the experiment?

04:13.481 --> 04:15.081
Mew lot come, too.

04:15.081 --> 04:17.441
I'll invite you, as a special favor.

04:17.441 --> 04:20.341
And I'll allow it, meow. 
Mew'd better be grateful.

04:20.341 --> 04:22.141
H-Hey. What's this about?

04:22.141 --> 04:24.051
I'm busy!

04:31.351 --> 04:32.791
This place will do.

04:32.791 --> 04:34.651
It brings back memories, meow.

04:34.931 --> 04:40.071
<i>This is where Zanoba and I abducted 
Linia and Pursena that one time.</i>

04:40.791 --> 04:45.911
<i>It's the first place I fought them, 
so I guess it is kind of nostalgic.</i>

04:46.371 --> 04:50.791
Master, do you suppose this 
is leading up to a rematch?

04:54.121 --> 04:55.811
It could be.

05:01.371 --> 05:02.261
Huh?

05:02.731 --> 05:05.711
We want the boss and the rest 
of mew to witness this.

05:05.981 --> 05:07.381
What are you going to do?

05:07.381 --> 05:11.751
Linia and I are going to settle 
which one of us is stronger.

05:11.751 --> 05:13.591
Whatever for?

05:13.591 --> 05:17.361
The winner will become the chief 
of the Doldia Tribe, meow.

05:18.511 --> 05:22.261
The Dedoldia and Adoldia 
are two separate clans.

05:22.261 --> 05:25.111
Couldn't you each be 
chief of one of them?

05:25.111 --> 05:28.211
That's what we'd been thinking, meow.

05:28.211 --> 05:32.361
Until we clobbered all the suitors who 
came for us last mating season, meow.

05:32.361 --> 05:37.011
We never did find a man stronger than us.

05:37.011 --> 05:42.491
So, the stronger one of us will be chief, 
and the other will live free.

05:42.491 --> 05:45.201
There's more to life than becoming chief.

05:45.201 --> 05:46.841
No hard feelings, meow.

05:46.841 --> 05:48.741
<i>What kind of sense does that make?</i>

05:48.741 --> 05:50.211
I understand.

05:50.211 --> 05:53.301
Go at it to your hearts' content 
if that will satisfy you.

05:53.301 --> 05:56.381
You're sure you want to 
help set up a fight?

05:56.381 --> 05:59.271
They'd still do it, 
even if I wasn't watching them.

05:59.271 --> 06:00.901
We owe mew one.

06:00.901 --> 06:02.271
Thanks.

06:04.021 --> 06:06.781
<i>I'd guess they're evenly matched.</i>

06:07.121 --> 06:11.541
<i>I'd better watch this, if only 
to prevent any accidents.</i>

06:12.461 --> 06:16.671
<i>And, not to be pedantic, 
but this isn't a fight. It's a duel.</i>

06:16.671 --> 06:19.021
<i>They're battling to settle a question.</i>

06:23.161 --> 06:28.081
<i>We're about to witness two beasts 
seriously try to kill each other.</i>

06:28.081 --> 06:31.731
Pursena, I've been meaning 
to say this for a while.

06:31.731 --> 06:34.061
The truth is, I can't stand mew!

06:34.061 --> 06:35.851
You took the words out of my mouth!

06:35.851 --> 06:40.901
You trailed after me like a 
baby sister when we were little,

06:40.901 --> 06:42.521
but you've gotten full 
of yourself lately!

06:42.521 --> 06:45.621
Excuse meow?! Mew were the baby sister!

06:45.621 --> 06:50.701
Did you forget that time mew wet yourself 
when we were four and I hid it?!

06:50.701 --> 06:54.001
They say an Adoldia remembers 
a debt for a hundred years.

06:54.001 --> 06:55.581
What a load of hooey, meow!

06:55.581 --> 06:58.741
I saved you when you fell in 
the river and nearly drowned!

06:58.741 --> 06:59.991
That made us even!

06:59.991 --> 07:03.621
Mew'll never find yourself a man 
with that ungrateful attitude!

07:03.621 --> 07:06.961
Only because <i>you</i> wiped 
out all our suitors!

07:06.961 --> 07:08.431
Pursena, you busybody!

07:08.431 --> 07:09.721
Linia, you idiot!

07:09.721 --> 07:11.171
Pursena, you...

07:11.171 --> 07:12.631
fatty!

07:13.181 --> 07:16.881
I... I am not fat!

07:25.711 --> 07:30.131
Whoa! Pursena rolls up like a heavy tank,
 and Linia sends her packing!

07:30.131 --> 07:33.871
Pursena's got the edge in strength, 
but Linia edges her out in speed!

07:33.871 --> 07:36.531
Pursena just let loose 
with a right straight!

07:36.531 --> 07:37.461
Linia's reeling!

07:37.461 --> 07:38.831
Pursena's not letting up!

07:38.831 --> 07:40.191
What will Linia do?!

07:40.191 --> 07:42.101
Will she run?! Will she hold her ground?!

07:42.101 --> 07:43.861
She held her ground!

07:43.861 --> 07:45.851
Linia dishes out a left jab! And another!

07:45.851 --> 07:47.531
Pursena can't take much more!

07:47.531 --> 07:50.501
But Pursena advances 
to meet Linia's right!

07:50.501 --> 07:54.341
Oh! There go Pursena's clothes!

07:51.021 --> 07:52.961
That was dirty!

07:54.341 --> 07:56.361
Can't show that on TV!

07:56.361 --> 07:58.651
What do you think, Zanoba?!

08:01.361 --> 08:03.681
Pursena goes for inside fighting!

08:03.681 --> 08:06.651
Pursena's punches are wearing 
away at Linia's legs!

08:06.651 --> 08:10.871
Will she fall prey to the earthbound 
champion, like a wingless butterfly?!

08:10.871 --> 08:13.061
But Linia just dug her fangs in!

08:13.061 --> 08:15.741
She's pulling Pursena down 
onto the ground with her!

08:15.741 --> 08:18.011
But Pursena has fangs, too!

08:18.011 --> 08:20.331
She's biting back!

08:20.331 --> 08:22.441
What an unseemly way to fight.

08:22.441 --> 08:25.121
You'd think they were brawling children.

08:25.121 --> 08:27.781
Well, yeah. That's another way to put it.

08:28.101 --> 08:34.051
Hey. How come you're goofing off when 
they're both taking this so seriously?

08:37.121 --> 08:38.621
Sorry about that.

08:55.891 --> 08:57.451
I win.

09:00.791 --> 09:05.181
<i>She was breathtaking. Magnificent.</i>

09:05.611 --> 09:08.631
<i>You could tell she'd triumphed 
after a brutal battle.</i>

09:15.881 --> 09:17.721
I won.

09:18.111 --> 09:20.191
Yes. Congratulations.

09:20.191 --> 09:22.071
I'll patch you up with a healing spell.

09:22.381 --> 09:25.201
Thanks, but I don't need it.

09:25.511 --> 09:27.721
These wounds are badges of honor.

09:27.721 --> 09:32.021
I don't know if I'll ever see Linia 
again, so I'll leave them be.

09:33.031 --> 09:36.671
Hang on. Won't you stick 
together until you leave town?

09:37.391 --> 09:39.341
This is where we part.

09:39.341 --> 09:42.851
We've already packed our stuff, 
so we'll leave within the day.

09:43.691 --> 09:46.781
<i>Did they agree on that ahead of time?</i>

09:46.781 --> 09:50.071
<i>To say goodbye here, 
where their paths diverge?</i>

09:52.251 --> 09:54.441
<i>That's kind of cool.</i>

09:55.171 --> 09:59.061
You should get yourself patched up, 
even if it's not with magic.

09:59.061 --> 10:00.681
I know.

10:00.681 --> 10:03.281
Boss, this is goodbye.

10:13.061 --> 10:15.521
<i>They both have their good sides.</i>

10:17.111 --> 10:18.051
<i>Now...</i>

10:22.451 --> 10:23.891
Are you alive?

10:25.141 --> 10:27.041
Yeah, I am, meow.

10:27.041 --> 10:29.081
So much for your good looks.

10:29.081 --> 10:30.741
Mew can say that again.

10:32.811 --> 10:34.671
Thanks, meow.

10:37.501 --> 10:39.341
I lost, meow.

10:39.341 --> 10:41.011
You fought well.

10:41.011 --> 10:43.801
I could hear mew the whole time, Boss.

10:43.801 --> 10:46.351
Mew sure were enjoying yourself.

10:46.661 --> 10:50.091
<i>I'll admit I maybe didn't do 
the best job reading the room.</i>

10:50.471 --> 10:53.011
<i>Still, they put on a good, 
exciting match.</i>

10:53.361 --> 10:57.041
Well, I'm glad you had fun one last time.

10:57.041 --> 10:59.821
It must've looked like a regular 
brawl to anybody else.

10:59.821 --> 11:01.911
You've gotta take your fun 
where mew can get it.

11:01.911 --> 11:04.141
No healing magic for you, either?

11:04.141 --> 11:07.601
Honestly, I'd like to 
erase the signs I lost.

11:07.601 --> 11:10.631
But, well, I'll take my 
lumps this time, meow.

11:10.631 --> 11:14.961
They'll still be something to brag 
about if I wait long enough.

11:14.961 --> 11:17.191
Those are honorable wounds.

11:17.191 --> 11:22.251
I don't know much of beast people 
duels, but I found yours riveting.

11:22.251 --> 11:25.021
I didn't figure on getting 
compliments from <i>mew</i>.

11:25.021 --> 11:28.261
It's a big change from the 
time mew kidnapped us here.

11:28.561 --> 11:31.271
Sorry about your doll, meow.

11:31.271 --> 11:34.781
My master already pardoned 
you for that incident.

11:34.781 --> 11:38.781
I no longer bear you any ill will.

11:44.411 --> 11:47.431
What are you gonna do now?

11:47.431 --> 11:51.051
Travel wherever the road takes me 
and go into business, meow.

11:51.331 --> 11:54.781
<i>Business, huh? 
I can't see that going well.</i>

11:55.021 --> 11:57.671
Do you have any specific plans?

11:57.671 --> 11:59.431
Mew bet I do.

11:59.431 --> 12:02.001
<i>If she has a vision, 
maybe it'll work out.</i>

12:02.611 --> 12:05.641
<i>Scratch that. I still can't see it.</i>

12:05.641 --> 12:10.811
<i>Something tells me she'll go off 
half-cocked and land herself in hot water.</i>

12:11.181 --> 12:14.941
I'm planning to be rolling in 
money five years from meow.

12:15.271 --> 12:20.101
Well, you know, I'll be here for 
you if you run into trouble.

12:20.101 --> 12:22.161
I will assist you as well.

12:23.081 --> 12:26.561
I'll give mew a loan once I hit it big.

12:29.801 --> 12:33.011
<i>Are they really never going 
to see each other again?</i>

12:33.481 --> 12:35.451
<i>I mean, they were inseparable.</i>

12:37.421 --> 12:43.301
<i>But I couldn't help feeling that 
was kind of a cool way to live.</i>

12:45.501 --> 12:49.071
<i>Later, a little bird told me</i>

12:45.581 --> 12:48.011
We said that was goodbye, meow!

12:48.011 --> 12:51.891
<i>You</i> followed <i>me!</i> Do something 
about that needy streak of yours!

12:49.071 --> 12:54.261
<i>about two bandaged beast women 
seen squabbling in a stagecoach.</i>

12:51.891 --> 12:54.271
<i>You're</i> the one who won't leave 
<i>me</i> alone! Get off, meow!

12:54.271 --> 12:55.681
No! You get off!

12:55.211 --> 13:00.121
<i>I bet they bumped into each other 
because they didn't check when it left.</i>

12:55.681 --> 12:56.311
You get off, meow!

12:56.311 --> 12:57.211
You get off, Linia!

12:57.211 --> 12:58.391
No, mew, Pursena!

12:58.391 --> 13:01.461
Linia! Linia! Linia!

13:00.121 --> 13:01.821
<i>Talk about an anticlimax.</i>

13:01.461 --> 13:02.761
Pursena, meow!

13:10.171 --> 13:12.141
Now, begin.

13:13.871 --> 13:15.901
I'm going to start injecting mana.

13:18.551 --> 13:21.471
<i>This thing takes a hell of a lot.</i>

13:21.471 --> 13:24.471
<i>Could anyone but me even use it?</i>

13:25.091 --> 13:26.791
This will take a while.

13:26.791 --> 13:28.721
Maybe we should work on improving—

13:27.751 --> 13:28.721
Shh!

13:34.951 --> 13:37.201
<i>I've seen a glow like this before.</i>

13:37.741 --> 13:41.851
<i>This is what I saw right 
before the mass teleportation.</i>

13:42.501 --> 13:44.411
<i>What does that mean? Should I stop?</i>

13:44.771 --> 13:46.841
<i>No one wants another disaster like that.</i>

13:47.991 --> 13:53.001
<i>No. We've put a lot of research into 
making sure that doesn't happen.</i>

13:53.591 --> 13:56.471
<i>We can do this. 
We have nothing to worry about.</i>

14:12.001 --> 14:13.171
Success!

14:14.091 --> 14:15.101
It...

14:15.101 --> 14:16.601
worked!

14:16.601 --> 14:18.831
Congratulations, Master!

14:18.831 --> 14:19.941
We did it!

14:19.941 --> 14:22.741
Still, those stripes 
look awfully sinister.

14:22.741 --> 14:24.621
Are you sure it's safe to hold?

14:24.621 --> 14:27.401
Yes, but be careful not to drop it.

14:27.401 --> 14:28.941
It's more fragile than it looks.

14:28.941 --> 14:33.461
Hey, Nanahoshi, that watermelon 
is from the other world, right?

14:33.461 --> 14:35.451
I mean, they probably 
don't exist here.

14:35.451 --> 14:36.791
Most likely.

14:36.791 --> 14:40.201
Anyway, I can't designate 
a precise target yet.

14:40.631 --> 14:43.711
I was actually trying to 
summon a cabbage.

14:43.961 --> 14:45.831
It's denser and heavier than I thought.

14:44.041 --> 14:47.571
<i>This world does have vegetables 
similar to cabbages.</i>

14:45.831 --> 14:47.681
That's because it's mostly liquid.

14:47.571 --> 14:51.191
<i>Could we really tell the difference 
from an other-world vegetable?</i>

14:47.681 --> 14:49.571
It's a nice sweet treat.

14:49.571 --> 14:51.321
Sweet? It doesn't look it.

14:51.591 --> 14:54.251
Now you mention it, I guess 
it doesn't look very appetizing.

14:51.801 --> 14:57.281
<i>Maybe our plan to summon a vegetable 
was flawed from the start.</i>

14:54.251 --> 14:57.601
But that's the rind. 
The inside is the sweet part.

14:57.601 --> 15:00.481
Just wait till I serve you some later.

15:00.901 --> 15:02.821
<i>No, it's fine.</i>

15:02.821 --> 15:05.961
<i>We summoned a watermelon 
when we wanted a cabbage,</i>

15:05.961 --> 15:08.231
<i>but I'd still call it a success.</i>

15:08.231 --> 15:11.811
If we've succeeded, 
we ought to celebrate tonight.

15:11.811 --> 15:13.621
Yeah, you're right about that.

15:13.951 --> 15:15.881
Cheers!

15:16.401 --> 15:18.761
<i>I don't know when it started,</i>

15:18.761 --> 15:21.901
<i>but we party whenever one of 
us has something to celebrate.</i>

15:22.461 --> 15:25.581
<i>We're down Linia and Pursena now, though.</i>

15:25.581 --> 15:28.631
<i>Roxy and Norn have taken their places.</i>

15:28.871 --> 15:32.891
<i>Badigadi isn't here, either, so we're 
missing the liveliest members,</i>

15:32.891 --> 15:35.751
<i>but I don't think the 
overall mood has changed.</i>

15:36.271 --> 15:40.221
<i>Anyway, it's not every day that
I see Nanahoshi that happy.</i>

15:40.221 --> 15:42.341
Here you go, Rudy.

15:42.341 --> 15:45.391
Thanks. Don't you want any?

15:45.391 --> 15:50.651
I get a little funny when I drink, 
so I don't want to overdo it.

15:50.651 --> 15:51.901
Oh, okay.

15:52.241 --> 15:54.361
We're not spending the 
night this time, remember.

15:54.361 --> 15:57.371
We're going home and 
tucking Lucie into bed.

15:57.371 --> 15:58.661
I know.

15:58.661 --> 16:02.031
<i>Drunk Sylphie is adorable, though.</i>

16:02.031 --> 16:03.241
Rudy.

16:03.661 --> 16:06.161
Pull out your chair out a little.

16:08.971 --> 16:10.981
Roxy, are you drunk?

16:10.981 --> 16:12.281
A little.

16:12.281 --> 16:14.671
I wish you'd do that for <i>me</i> later.

16:14.671 --> 16:16.131
Of course I will.

16:16.421 --> 16:21.511
<i>Hell, I wouldn't mind having Roxy 
on my left and Sylphie on my right.</i>

16:21.511 --> 16:22.581
Brother.

16:24.391 --> 16:27.591
Sorry, Norn. Am I embarrassing you?

16:27.591 --> 16:29.281
No, it's fine.

16:29.611 --> 16:34.021
I, uh, wanted to talk about something. 
Do you have a moment?

16:34.341 --> 16:35.911
Sure. What is it?

16:35.911 --> 16:40.401
Okay. You see, it's about 
the student council.

16:40.701 --> 16:42.191
Oh, I see.

16:42.191 --> 16:47.111
<i>Come to think of it, Norn was 
with them at graduation.</i>

16:47.381 --> 16:49.881
Ariel invited me to join.

16:50.741 --> 16:53.971
My grades aren't the best,

16:53.971 --> 16:58.641
but she said I have a gift 
for drawing people to me.

16:58.641 --> 16:59.961
You don't say.

16:59.961 --> 17:03.751
<i>I have heard that Norn has 
a lot of fans at school.</i>

17:03.751 --> 17:05.811
Did you know, Sylphie?

17:05.811 --> 17:07.521
Yup. More or less.

17:07.521 --> 17:09.461
<i>So, she knew about it.</i>

17:09.461 --> 17:11.211
<i>Maybe Roxy did, too.</i>

17:13.061 --> 17:15.181
<i>Was I the only one in the dark?</i>

17:15.181 --> 17:16.601
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

17:16.601 --> 17:20.551
Sorry. I thought Norn 
should ask you herself.

17:20.551 --> 17:21.701
Oh, okay.

17:22.231 --> 17:27.341
So... would you mind if I officially 
joined the student council?

17:27.341 --> 17:28.591
Of course—

17:28.591 --> 17:33.121
<i>Wait. Norn is working on swordplay 
and writing right now.</i>

17:33.121 --> 17:37.091
<i>Can she handle student council 
work on top of that?</i>

17:37.671 --> 17:38.781
Norn.

17:38.781 --> 17:39.771
Yes?

17:39.771 --> 17:45.221
I'm not against you joining the council,
as long as it's not too much to take on.

17:45.611 --> 17:49.391
I'm sure your schoolwork will be more 
difficult as you start your third year.

17:49.811 --> 17:53.741
I'll work hard at writing and 
sword fighting and school, too.

17:54.141 --> 17:57.381
<i>That's easy to say. Still...</i>

17:58.861 --> 17:59.941
Rudy.

18:01.111 --> 18:04.581
Norn has been keeping on top 
of her responsibilities.

18:04.581 --> 18:08.311
And she's been helping the 
student council for over a year now.

18:08.311 --> 18:09.371
Huh?

18:09.371 --> 18:13.531
You mean, since before I started 
teaching her to use a sword?

18:14.351 --> 18:17.791
She'll be fine, Rudy. I guarantee it.

18:18.601 --> 18:21.691
<i>I get it. This isn't about 
whether she can do it.</i>

18:21.691 --> 18:23.561
<i>She proved she could before she asked.</i>

18:23.561 --> 18:26.301
<i>In that case, who am I to tell her no?</i>

18:26.661 --> 18:28.811
You've been working hard, huh, Norn?

18:29.211 --> 18:33.581
I don't think you need my permission, 
 but you've got it anyway.

18:34.551 --> 18:36.321
Thank you so much!

18:37.771 --> 18:39.741
Attention, everybody!

18:39.741 --> 18:41.821
Time to cut the watermelon!

18:41.821 --> 18:45.081
<i>In the end, it comes 
down to her own effort.</i>

18:45.561 --> 18:49.801
<i>Nanahoshi gets results because 
she's putting in the work, too.</i>

18:49.801 --> 18:51.831
<i>The same goes for Linia and Pursena.</i>

18:52.121 --> 18:56.721
<i>But I think all of us have 
a duty to cheer them on.</i>

18:56.981 --> 19:01.271
<i>I wouldn't be who I am now if the
 people in my life hadn't supported me.</i>

19:01.841 --> 19:05.421
<i>So, I'll always be ready 
to support them, too.</i>

19:10.471 --> 19:12.131
Thanks for—

19:12.831 --> 19:14.351
Are you okay?

19:15.121 --> 19:17.021
Want me to cast detoxification?

19:17.521 --> 19:20.991
I got Sylphie to do it earlier, 
so I'm good for now.

19:21.261 --> 19:23.891
Anyway, you were a big 
help again this time.

19:23.891 --> 19:26.231
I can finally move on 
to the next phase now.

19:26.631 --> 19:31.171
That's about specifying exactly 
what you summon, right?

19:31.171 --> 19:35.621
Right. I know an expert in that, 
so I'm going to go ask him.

19:35.621 --> 19:39.141
<i>The good old 
"authority on summoning," huh?</i>

19:41.141 --> 19:44.111
You don't mean Orsted, do you?

19:44.111 --> 19:45.571
Not him.

19:46.981 --> 19:52.521
So, just a suggestion, but you know how 
I still owe you for an old experiment?

19:52.521 --> 19:56.201
Oh, now that you mention it, 
I was so busy, we put off payment.

19:56.201 --> 20:02.111
How about I introduce you to that mage 
to cover it all, today included?

20:02.111 --> 20:03.921
An introduction, huh?

20:03.921 --> 20:07.871
But is he really such a big deal that 
meeting him's worth two rewards?

20:07.871 --> 20:12.371
Yes. There's a chance he 
could even do something

20:12.371 --> 20:14.641
about your mother's memory loss.

20:15.671 --> 20:17.121
What?

20:17.431 --> 20:20.141
You really mean that?

20:20.391 --> 20:25.391
I can't be sure, but he's lived a long 
time, so there is a good chance.

20:27.111 --> 20:30.481
<i>I think Zenith is making 
a steady recovery,</i>

20:30.481 --> 20:34.051
<i>but it's hard to know if she'll 
ever get her memory back.</i>

20:34.471 --> 20:36.201
<i>Even if he can't cure her,</i>

20:36.201 --> 20:41.201
<i>knowing what to call her condition 
and some similar cases could be useful.</i>

20:42.121 --> 20:44.391
Since you're only telling me now,

20:44.391 --> 20:46.941
I assume there's a reason your 
couldn't introduce us sooner?

20:46.941 --> 20:50.361
There is. Sorry, but I have 
my own stuff to deal with.

20:50.711 --> 20:53.881
Are you referring to 
your master in magic?

20:53.881 --> 20:58.251
If you're offering introductions, 
I'd like to meet him, too.

20:58.251 --> 20:59.271
Well...

20:59.271 --> 21:02.651
You did help me, too, 
so I guess I don't mind.

21:02.651 --> 21:03.631
Um...

21:03.631 --> 21:05.971
I'm a bit curious, too.

21:05.971 --> 21:09.371
Won't we bother him if we 
all go at once, though?

21:09.371 --> 21:11.001
That's all right.

21:11.001 --> 21:13.721
He said he can handle up to twelve.

21:13.721 --> 21:16.841
But won't going to see him take time?

21:16.841 --> 21:19.231
I can get to him in a day if I want.

21:19.231 --> 21:21.491
Wow. So, he's local?

21:21.491 --> 21:24.051
Have we already met, by any chance?

21:24.051 --> 21:28.601
He's not local, and you haven't 
met him, but I know a way to.

21:28.601 --> 21:30.111
I... see.

21:30.391 --> 21:32.961
Well then, what's this guy's name?

21:38.241 --> 21:41.471
I want you to keep this private. Okay?

21:45.301 --> 21:47.511
He's Perugius, the Armored Dragon King.

21:49.621 --> 21:51.761
<i>Perugius, the Armored Dragon King.</i>

21:52.111 --> 21:55.761
<i>That was the name of one of the 
three heroes who killed the Demon God</i>

21:55.761 --> 22:01.231
<i>and led humanity to victory in the 
Laplace War four hundred years ago.</i>

22:02.031 --> 22:05.031
<b>Episode 7
Phase Four</b>

23:35.041 --> 23:40.121
Next Time
The Flying Fortress
